.Rproj.user
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata

# Raw (unzipped) CSVs stay ignored so a working gunzip never lands a 60+ MB diff by accident.
# The dataset itself IS committed, as data/labels-*-latlng.csv.gz — a reconstruction from
# production; see data/MANIFEST.md and issue #1. (This pattern does not match *.csv.gz.)
data/*.csv
data/depth-pilot-cache/
scripts/*_cache/

__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# Python environments built by scripts/setup_venv.py. The versions that define them belong
# in python/requirements.txt, which IS committed; the installed tree never is. The glob
# covers the per-platform variants a checkout shared between Windows and WSL needs
# (.venv-win, .venv-wsl, ...), since a venv cannot span the two.
.venv*/
venv/

# The depth-validation fetch cache (raw tiles + photometa). The committed
# data/depth-validation-tiles.jsonl.gz holds the same tile bytes verbatim, so `build`
# and every downstream stage replay offline without it.
data/depth-validation-cache/

# Modern-truth working data (issue #3): the raw all-city extraction (~1.2M rows, regenerable
# via scripts/extraction/extract-modern-labels.sh) and the photometa fetch cache. Only the
# sampled subset is committed, as data/modern-truth-*.gz; see data/MANIFEST.md.
data/modern-extraction/
data/modern-truth-cache/

# The conclusions-page tile fetch cache (issue #7 viz). The committed
# data/triangulation-viz-tiles.jsonl.gz holds the same bytes verbatim, so `build`
# replays offline without it.
data/triangulation-viz-cache/

# The overlay gallery is generated from the committed tiles by `run_depth_validation.py
# gallery`; 8 MB of regenerable HTML does not belong in history.
figures/depth-overlay-gallery.html
